::PC_U02_L04_Q01::
Question ID: PC_U02_L04_Q01
MLA Standard: MLA.PC.FA.5
Question:
In a rational model, which statement best supports the 
{
=A. Check where the denominator equals 0 and connect it to the context.#Correct. Denominator restrictions are central to rational model interpretation.
~B. Use every real number because rational functions have fractions.#Fractions create restrictions when the denominator is 0.
~C. Ignore restrictions if the numerator is positive.#A positive numerator does not remove denominator restrictions.
~D. Use only the y-intercept to interpret the model.#The y-intercept may help, but it does not replace domain analysis.
}
